# OpenVOD — environment variable reference (summary)
#
# Full per-service guidance:
#   server/.dev.vars.example   — API env (copy to server/.dev.vars)
#   delivery/.dev.vars.example — delivery worker env
#   web/ (NEXT_PUBLIC_*)       — dashboard env (Vercel project or Docker ARG)
#   README.md + docs/          — quickstarts, deployment, security model
#
# Interactive BYOK wizard — writes server/.dev.vars + delivery/.dev.vars:
#   ./scripts/bootstrap.sh        # --force to regenerate, --deploy to provision
# Validate what is configured (no secrets printed):
#   scripts/verify-env.sh
# Live readiness (no secrets returned):
#   curl <api>/health/config

# ── Public env vars baked into the dashboard at build time ────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787/api
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787/api/auth
NEXT_PUBLIC_FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Docker (docker compose up -d) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# postgres, api and web boot together; the API migrates the schema before
# listening. Override the defaults below when you need to:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@postgres:5432/vod_dev
#   JWT_SECRET=change-me-32-chars-min
#   BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=change-me-32-chars-min
# Real R2/Modal values are read from server/.dev.vars when present.
